-- title:
--   Chart automorphism agrees with the field automorphism σ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, i.e. every unit $u$ with `ZMod.unitsMap` image $1$ lies in $H$. Assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the rational image of the integral power series $E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}$-numerator `jNum`, lies in the full-level field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms. For a congruence subgroup $\Gamma$, `chartAlgFin p Γ hj` denotes the subalgebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ` integral over the $(R\,p)$-subalgebra generated by the element `jAt Γ hj`. Given: an $(R\,p)$-algebra map $\iota_0$ from the chart ring at level `ΓN p M H hpM` to that at level `ΓM M H` preserving underlying Laurent series; an $(R\,p)$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of the chart ring at level `ΓM M H` with $\theta(\iota_0 b)$ having Laurent series `qExpand ℚ p` of that of $b$, where `qExpand ℚ p` multiplies exponents by $p$, i.e. $f(q) \mapsto f(q^p)$; and a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` such that whenever $f$ there and $u$ in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓN p M H hpM)` have equal Laurent series, $\sigma f$ has Laurent series $u(q^p)$. Then for every $b$ in the chart ring at level `ΓM M H`, the image of $\theta b$ in the function field equals $\sigma$ applied to the image of $b$.
--
--   This is the rigidity step identifying the chart-level automorphism $\theta$ of the $j$-finite chart ring of the two-chart integral model at $p$ with the Atkin–Lehner-type automorphism $\sigma$ of the $q$-expansion function field: agreement on the subring coming from the smaller level, where both are $q \mapsto q^p$, forces agreement on the whole chart ring. It feeds the construction of the retraction and the description of supersingular points in [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_retraction_tmul_theta_eq_zero_and_mem_iff_exists_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_retraction_tmul_theta_eq_zero_and_mem_iff_exists_mem_ssJSet) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.retraction_map_theta_eq_zero_mem_of_mem_ssJSet_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.retraction_map_theta_eq_zero_mem_of_mem_ssJSet_gammaH).
